=2 Walkthrough
* __(Optional)__ Speak to {n:Andreine} in the {z:Celennia Memorial Library} for a hint regarding Oshasha's whereabouts.
* Travel to {z:Leafallia} and interact with the **Odyssean Passage** for a cutscene.
* Trade a {@i:Stygian Ash|19210} {p:Stygian Ash} to the **Odyssean Passage** for another cutscene. You will receive {@k} {k:Bronze-hued tag}.
** {@i:Stygian Ash|19210} {p:Stygian Ash} drops from the {p:Pixie|Category:Pixie} family, which are easily found in {z:Grauberg (S)} around **Witchfire Glen**.
*** The most accessible way to get to Witchfire Glen is using your {k:Lightsworm} on the blue sparkles near {z:Batallia Downs} Survival Guide. Once in Walk of Echoes, turn around and interact with the conflux just behind you to teleport to Witchfire Glen.
*** Alternatively, either Campaign Warp to {z:Grauberg} or use the {p:Survival Guide}.
*** {s:Recall-Pashh} will also bring you near the conflux in {z:Pashhow Marshlands (S)} which you may also use teleport to Witchfire Glen, but it requires you complete late game voidwatch quests.
* Travel to {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar} (K-3), Upper Floor (map 1). (Via waypoint to Outer Ra'Kaznar)
** To get here, it is easy to follow the marked path on the {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar} page's maps.
** **DO NOT** interact with the roots at (J-3), continue over to (K-3) when you reach that spot. __Otherwise you will be forced to take a teleport to the entrance and run through the entire area again.__
* Interact with the **Shrouded Workroom** at (K-3) for a cutscene.
** Be careful, as there are {p:Umbrils|Umbril} around the area.
* Return to {z:Leafallia} and interact with the **Odyssean Passage** for the final cutscene and your reward, completing the mission.
* Continue with the creation of your Prime Weapon by following the section below. You will need it to progress in the coming quests.

!Updated marked map outer ra'kaznar map 1.jpeg||Ground Floor
!Updated marked map outer ra'kaznar map 2.jpeg||Basement
=2 Notes
* At this point, you can now open up access to two new {p:Records of Eminence} objectives. See the NPC {n:Elijah} in {z:Upper Jeuno} near Home Point #1 for more information.
* **{c=red:Caution:}** You will need a {p:Prime Weapon} that can deal damage (**NOT** the Shield or Instrument!) for future missions, so make sure to create one at some point.

=2 Starting your Prime Weapon
* Speak to {p:Oggbi} in {z:Port Bastok} (E-6) Homepoint #3 in the Steaming Sheep after the mission for a cutscene.
** You will receive {@k} {k:Uran-Mafran's orb} after the cutscene.
* Return to {n:Gama-Shama} in the {z:Silver Knife}, he will ask for 10k {p:Gallimaufry} to choose your Prime Weapon.
** There is a game day wait afterwards.
** You can purchase multiple Prime Weapons as long as you have the {p:Gallimaufry} to do so.

=3 A Word on Choosing Your Weapon
You will need a Prime Weapon upgraded to stage 2 to be able to enter the final mission fight of this storyline. Your choice will limit the jobs you can take to that fight!
* The fight is more difficult than every other fight in The Voracious Resurgence, and you will probably need the help of other players.

If you do not intend to forge your Prime Weapon all the way to the final stage, and you have a support job you may want to use later, it is best to choose the melee weapon for that job:
* {@i:Lorg Mor (Level 119 III)|21998} {i:Lorg Mor|Lorg Mor|21998} for WHM or GEO.
* {@i:Opashoro (Level 119 III)|22103} {i:Opashoro|Opashoro|22103} for BLM, SMN, or SCH.
* {@i:Mpu Gandring (Level 119 III)|21587} {i:Mpu Gandring|Mpu Gandring|21587} for RDM, THF, BRD, or DNC.
* {@i:Caliburnus (Level 119 III)|21643} {i:Caliburnus|Caliburnus|21643} for PLD, BLU, or RDM.
** Other job selections can be seen on the {p:Prime Weapons} page.

